//
// Research Modal Build C, spec §8: the in-battle sheet on a phone, from
// committed JSON fixtures shaped from real battle documents (the measured
// position generated by the real corrected-battle harness, scorer and committed
// patch; no production read). `?sheetFixture=held_tf|held_cp|held_legacy|bench_incumbent|unexamined|budget_out|held_redzone`.
// `held_redzone` (founder ruling FQ-9, 2026-11-08): the sheet AND Bomb mode on, AAPL
// at $103.40 — 0.36 % under the +30 rung with the market open — so the modal opens on
// 💣 in the red zone, not the sheet.
//
// The page fixes the clock to the fixture's instant (Wed Oct 14 2026, 1:07 PM
// ET), answers /api/stocks/historical and /api/stocks/fundamentals from
// generated data, and mounts the real AssetResearchModal exactly as the Battle
// View's shipped mount does, with the sheetContext the screen builds — the
// battle, its calls and the rankings handed over (no Firestore read). THE ASK
// IS ANSWERED HERE by a canned reply marked SMOKE ONLY: no model is called and
// no budget is charged anywhere; the page then adds the exchange to its own
// copy of the battle so the "filed to chat" chip can light.
//
// MEASUREMENT PARAMETERS (SMOKE ONLY — for the fold check and the review's
// worst cases; none changes the fixtures above unless asked):
//   ?name=…   the agent's name (the app caps it at 20 characters)
//   ?arch=…   the equipped archetype (e.g. analyst)
//   ?long=1   a long rationale sentence, idea statement and directive
//   ?bars=1   weekly and 30-minute bars too (for 1W and 💣)
//   ?bomb=1   Bomb mode on as well (the screen's bombContext; implies ?bars=1)
//   ?delay=N  every series answers N ms late (the skeleton)
//   ?fail=1   every series fails (the error box)

